WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.980
Safe process invocation in Bash is a repeatable checklist.

2
00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:08.360
Start by choosing known executables and reviewed tools.

3
00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:10.940
Avoid arbitrary command names from input.

4
00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:18.080
Understand how PATH, wrappers, helper scripts, and versions affect what program actually runs.

5
00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:26.260
Arbitrary command names, inherited secrets, ambiguous working directories, and ignored failures can make process execution unpredictable.

6
00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:29.100
Pass arguments separately.

7
00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:32.080
Quote variables that should remain single values.

8
00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:35.700
Use arrays when building options and operands.

9
00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:38.280
Use "$@" when forwarding an argument list.

10
00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:44.300
Avoid command strings when the real model is executable plus structured arguments.

11
00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:46.820
Control runtime context.

12
00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:50.200
Treat environment variables as process input.

13
00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:53.820
Avoid leaking secrets to tools that do not need them.

14
00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:56.160
Be explicit about current working directory.

15
00:00:56.260 --> 00:00:58.580
Validate input and output paths.

16
00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:03.320
Handle standard input, standard output, standard error, and redirection intentionally.

17
00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:04.720
Check results.

18
00:01:04.820 --> 00:01:14.180
Define success clearly, inspect exit status where it matters, and make pipeline behavior explicit when upstream failure would change the meaning of the run.

19
00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:17.560
Use timeouts and retry limits for unattended work.

20
00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:21.900
Treat background process ownership and cleanup as part of the design.

21
00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:24.900
Use least privilege and log safely.

22
00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:30.040
Scope service accounts, permissions, and delegated privilege rules to the job.

23
00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:33.900
Record useful actions and failures without exposing sensitive data.

24
00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:41.840
Review scripts with ShellCheck, peer review, CI/CD linting, staged rollout, and realistic tests before trusting them in production.
